/T (RIGHT JOIN: returns all rows from the right table, even if there are no matches in the left table.  FULL JOIN: returns rows when there is a match in one of the tables.  SELF JOIN: is used to join a table to itself, as if the table were two tables, temporarily renaming at least one table in the SQL statement.  CARTESIAN JOIN: returns the cartesian product of the sets of records from the two or more joined tables. )
